{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:503-516` and `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:744-752` stop scaling `filter.media_area_cm2`, but seeded scenarios still have no way to supply a replacement hardware-specific value (`crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:220-234`, `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1864-1877`). Because `FilterHardware::default()` hard-codes 2000 cm2 (`crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs:77-90`), every seeded tank now materializes with the same filter-media habitat area regardless of size while flow still scales with volume. That collapses size-dependent biofilter/habitat differences and makes startup scenarios ecologically incorrect. Restore geometry scaling or add an explicit scenario/startup media-area parameter before removing the old rule.","rationale":"I verified the current materialization path and both `nano_cycle` and `medium_planted` seed with `media_area_cm2 = 2000`, so the new comment about preserving a 'scenario-authored value' is not achievable with the current preset/override model."},{"body":"`crates/tank_core/tests/end_to_end.rs:257-289` weakens `happy_plants_grow_with_light_and_nutrients` from a growth assertion to an `>= 80%` survivability check without fixing the underlying regression. The test name and doc comment still say plants grow under good light and nutrients, but the suite now passes even when that happy-path scenario loses 20% of its biomass. This removes an important end-to-end guard for a user-visible regression instead of addressing the cause.","rationale":"Running `cargo test -p tank_core happy_plants_grow_with_light_and_nutrients -- --nocapture` on this diff produced about 19.24 g from an initial ~24 g after 30 days, so the new threshold is actively masking a failing scenario rather than documenting equivalent behavior."}],"summary":"Found two issues: removing filter-media scaling hard-codes the same 2000 cm2 filter habitat into every seeded scenario, and the end-to-end plant test was loosened to hide a regression instead of fixing it."}